<title>USA: Interline Resources Corp Q4 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Interline Resources Corp Q4 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>ALPINE, Utah 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter ended  Fiscal year ended</p>
<p>				  Dec. 31,		Dec. 31,</p>
<p>			  1996	  1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Revenue	 $3,665,722  $8,095,498 $17,011,792 $20,405,802</p>
<p>Operating Income</p>
<p>	  (loss)(2,143,631)   (493,266) (3,904,775)     146,528</p>
<p>Net Income (loss)</p>
<p>		  (2,158,039)   (622,226) (4,612,332)   (433,094)</p>
<p>Income (loss) per share</p>
<p>			  (.15)	 (.04)	 (.33)	 (.03)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for fiscal 1996 includes write-downs of $293,118 for the assets of a joint venture in England called Interline (U.K.) and $265,000 for the value of a pilot plant for the research and development of patented used oil refining technology.</p>
<p>The company said it has discontinued the commercial construction division of Gagon Mechanical Inc.</p>
